# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY (BC3). Never commit a real value to this file.
# The real values live in GitHub repo secrets and in Apps Script Script Properties.

# Q2 - the client's real domain. Absolute URLs (canonical, hreflang, OG, sitemap,
# JSON-LD) are all derived from this, so a wrong value ships wrong SEO.
#
# CAVEAT, LOCAL ONLY: a value here does NOT change the origin during `npm run dev`
# or a local `npm run build`. astro.config.mjs is evaluated BEFORE Astro loads
# .env, so `site:` falls back to its own default and the emitted canonicals read
# https://getcartravel.uz regardless of what you put here. The other three vars
# below are read from src/config/site.ts at render time and DO pick .env up.
# To override the origin locally, put it on the command line instead:
#   SITE_URL=https://staging.example npm run build
# In CI it works either way — deploy.yml exports it as a real process env var.
SITE_URL=https://example.uz

# §9.3 - the Apps Script Web App /exec URL, deployed under the CLIENT'S account.
LEAD_ENDPOINT=https://script.google.com/macros/s/REPLACE_ME/exec

# §9.5 - a bot filter, NOT authentication. Readable in the bundle by design.
# Must match FORM_TOKEN in Apps Script Script Properties.
LEAD_TOKEN=replace-me

# Q8 - Yandex Metrica counter id. Requires a YANDEX account, not a Google one.
# Any counter satisfies Gate 1; the client's real counter is a Gate-2 item.
METRICA_ID=00000000
